            <ArticleTitle>Case report: renal osteodystrophy in association with spinal stenosis in achondroplasia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 54 year old woman with achondroplasia presented with symptoms of spinal stenosis. Subsequent studies revealed end-stage renal disease with severe renal osteodystrophy that was characterised by radiographs and new bone biomarkers. We speculate that renal osteodystrophy accentuated spinal stenosis, which is a common feature of achondroplasia in adults.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
